\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{A row calculation on the three-by-three torus}
\date{2026-11-19}

\p{On the [periodic square lattice](fdip-006M) of periods three, take
uniform real edge coupling #{w} and uniform external field #{\eta}
in the direction of a reference unit spin. For the sign model label
each spin by #{a=\pm1}. For the three-state clock label it by
#{a\in\mathbb Z/3\mathbb Z}, with the reference spin at #{0}. Write
#{B(a,b)} for the spin inner product and #{u(a)} for the component
along the reference spin. Their numerical values are
##{\begin{aligned}
 \text{sign:}\quad & B(a,b)=ab,\qquad u(a)=a,\\
 \text{clock:}\quad & B(a,b)=\cos(2\pi(a-b)/3),\\
 & u(a)=\cos(2\pi a/3).
\end{aligned}}}

\p{Let #{A} be the set of rows of three labels. For rows
#{a,b\in A}, indices #{i} are read modulo three. Put
##{\begin{aligned}
 H(a)&=\sum_i B(a_i,a_{i+1}),&
 C(a,b)&=\sum_i B(a_i,b_i),\\
 u_{\rm row}(a)&=\sum_i u(a_i).
\end{aligned}}
Define the row operator #{\transferop_\eta} on real functions of
#{A} by its kernel in the row-indicator basis,
##{\transferop_\eta(a,b)=
 \ue^{w H(a)+\eta u_{\rm row}(a)+w C(a,b)}.}
Thus #{(\transferop_\eta f)(a)=\sum_{b\in A}\transferop_\eta(a,b)f(b)}.
Let #{M_u} multiply a row function by #{u(a_0)}. Then at any vertex
#{x} the partition and the mean component along the field are
##{Z(\eta)=\trace(\transferop_\eta^3),\qquad
 \langle u(\phi_x)\rangle_\eta=
 \frac{\trace(M_u\transferop_\eta^3)}{\trace(\transferop_\eta^3)}.}
Here #{u(\phi_x)} means the component of the spin with its indicated
label. For the sign this component is the field itself. In the clock
model reflection in the reference axis preserves each factor and
reverses the perpendicular component. Thus the full mean equals
the displayed component times the reference spin.}

\p{Indeed, expanding the trace sums over ordered rows #{a,b,c} the
product #{\transferop_\eta(a,b)\transferop_\eta(b,c)\transferop_\eta(c,a)}.
This counts each of the #{9} sites, #{9} horizontal links and #{9}
vertical links once. Inserting #{M_u} measures the first site of row
#{a}. Translations give the same mean at every site. The row spaces
have dimensions #{8} and #{27}. At #{\eta=0} the means vanish by
\ref{fdip-00ZY}. At #{w=0} the sites are independent. Their single-site
partitions and means along the reference direction are respectively
##{\begin{aligned}
 \text{sign:}\quad &2\cosh\eta,\qquad \tanh\eta,\\
 \text{clock:}\quad &\ue^{\eta}+2\ue^{-\eta /2},\qquad
 \frac{\ue^{\eta}-\ue^{-\eta /2}}{\ue^{\eta}+2\ue^{-\eta /2}}.
\end{aligned}}
The torus partition is the ninth power of the corresponding
single-site partition.}

\p{For an integer-weight calculation give an edge factor #{2} for
equal spins and #{1} otherwise. Give a site factor #{2} for the
reference spin and #{1} otherwise. In the same row sum the kernel
entry is #{2^{j(a)+j_0(a)+\ell(a,b)}}, where #{j(a)} counts equal
horizontal neighbors, #{j_0(a)} counts reference spins and #{\ell(a,b)}
counts matching columns. For each row #{a} form the sum
#{z(a)=\sum_{b,c}\transferop(a,b)\transferop(b,c)\transferop(c,a)}.
Grouping by the first spin gives
##{\begin{array}{c|r|r}
 &\sum_{a_0\ {\rm reference}}z(a)&\sum_{a_0\ {\rm other}}z(a)\\ \hline
 \text{sign}&181730304&10865664\\
 \text{clock}&254508320&38808320
\end{array}}
Thus the partition coefficients are #{192595968} and #{293316640}.
The nonreference spins have component #{-1} and #{-1/2} respectively,
giving means #{1030/1161} and #{1469401/1833229} along the field.}
